id: pm-7c27ep
title: "The tracker's recurrence edges and the CI recurrence policy are two ledgers with no join, so 59 of the 75 items in a recorded recurrence lineage produce no gate anywhere"
description: "Two capabilities shipped separately and were never connected.\n\npm-ouyq3n gave the relationship lexicon a recurs_from kind so a defect family fixed thirty times stops being thirty unrelated nodes. pm-1qkivy gave the repository a defect recurrence policy that turns resolved incident patterns into targeted local and hosted CI protections. Both are closed and both work. Nothing joins them.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-30 across all 2,602 items and the 8 families in config/defect-recurrence-policy.json. The record holds 52 recurs_from edges spanning 75 distinct items. The policy's families, counting owner, trigger and historical item ids together, name 16 of those 75. So 59 items sit in a recurrence lineage the tracker can already traverse and are covered by no family, which means no local check and no hosted check fires when their files are touched. Of those 59, 54 are closed and 5 are open.\n\nThe absence is structural rather than an oversight in one file. Outside src/types.ts, the relationship-kind contract, and graph governance, the string recurs_from does not appear anywhere in the repository. No gate, no script, and no policy validator reads the tracker's recurrence edges. Family registration is therefore an act of memory: someone has to notice a recurrence, remember the policy exists, and hand-write a family, and nothing fails when they do not.\n\nThis is the mechanism behind two recurrences observed on the same day this was measured. pm-4o7tlx is a verbatim recurrence of pm-t7wn04, a preflight gate red on a workstation and green in hosted CI for the same commit. pm-edywqn is the eighth measured instance of the family in which a checker enumerates its own hand-maintained list instead of iterating the artifact the outside world resolves. Both lineages were recordable as recurs_from edges and neither had a family, so neither had a gate, so both were rediscovered by hand.\n\nIt is also why the recurrence policy cannot answer its own governing question. The policy declares per-family escape-rate budgets, but an escape rate computed over registered families alone measures the families someone remembered to register. The denominator that matters is every recurrence the record can see."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:ci",denominator,governance,graph,recurrence
created_at: "2026-08-30T11:09:10.152Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T12:59:35.143Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T12:59:34.616Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T12:59:34.616Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The recurrence policy's family coverage is computed against the tracker's recurs_from lineages rather than against itself, so the covered and uncovered populations are both reported; An item that acquires a recurs_from edge and belongs to no registered family is surfaced as a named finding by a gate that already runs, rather than depending on someone remembering the policy exists; Registering a family is possible from the recorded lineage without hand-transcribing item ids, so the join is derived from the record rather than restated in a second file; Escape-rate budgets are reported against the full recurrence population the record can see, and a budget computed over registered families alone is labelled as such; A negative control proves the finding fires when a recurrence lineage is deliberately left unregistered, and does not fire for an item with no recurrence edge; The coverage computation stays inside the graph analytics token and latency budgets and remains bounded at million-item scale"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: "Join recorded local recurrence components to seeded policies and inherited item/file checks, preserve reversible incremental evidence, and reject incomplete workspace sources through the public strict-list contract. Expose bounded coverage consistently through SDK, CLI, MCP, and the mandatory defect gate."
expected_result: A complete recorded recurrence population selects family checks or fails with named findings; unreadable source items cannot disappear into a successful denominator.
actual_result: "Strict-source policy gate covers all 135 members / 46 components / 92 edges. The linked recurrence test command passes including corrupted-source SDK and CLI refusals. Prior full suite passed 8495 tests at 100/100/100/100; final full validation follows on the review head. Million-item and token ceilings remain unchanged. Review corrections: linked tests pass, normalization regressions fail on the previous source and pass after correction, action schemas match capability semantics, and all 56 token surfaces pass with existing ceilings unchanged. Final hosted checks are required before merge."
