comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T11:09:42.251Z","harness:claude-code","Two families were registered by hand in the same pass that measured this gap, which is the behaviour this item asks to make unnecessary rather than a fix for it.\n\nAdded to config/defect-recurrence-policy.json:\n- declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list, owner pm-suhxny, escape class production_defect, historical lineage pm-b84irw, pm-te6elw, pm-1jrdri, pm-6j7r1a, pm-xpumg4, pm-7wx1f9, pm-suhxny, pm-edywqn. Eight measured instances, the largest recurrence family in the record, previously unregistered.\n- ambient-host-state-in-measured-fixture, owner pm-4o7tlx, escape class review_caught_late, historical lineage pm-t7wn04 and pm-4o7tlx.\n\nSelection proven against the built SDK with analyzeDefectChangeRisk over the parsed policy. A change touching src/mcp/legacy-adapter.ts selects declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list, review-caught-contract-drift and security-scanner-finding. A change touching scripts/release/token-budget-gate.mjs selects ambient-host-state-in-measured-fixture and cross-platform-nightly-regression. A change touching sdk/public-surface.json selects declared-set-versus-hand-maintained-list. The negative control, a change touching only README.md, selects nothing, so the triggers discriminate rather than matching everything.\n\nPolicy validation and the scale benchmark both accept the additions: defect-evidence-gate reports PASS with 8 families and 0 findings, and defect-recurrence-index --check passes at 1,000,000 items with full 18.7s and incremental 25ms.\n\nCoverage after the additions is 16 of the 75 items in a recurrence lineage. Registering the remaining 59 by hand is not the fix and is not proposed here; deriving family coverage from the recorded lineages is."
  "2026-09-06T10:22:50.114Z","harness:codex","Complete all-status corpus census: 135 unique recorded recurrence members in 46 components and 92 directed local edges. Only 28 members inherit explicit existing family seeds; 107 are unregistered. There are no missing local targets. 74 members lack an explicit recognized escape classification, so the population escape rate must remain unknown, with an explicitly named lower bound. Register semantic component seeds and derive membership from actual recurs_from edges; do not infer coverage from matching tags or file globs."
  "2026-09-06T10:40:15.095Z","harness:codex","Verification: the mandatory recurrence-policy gate passes with 18 seeded families covering all 135 recorded recurrence members across 46 components and 92 edges. The million-item index benchmark passes unchanged latency/memory ceilings: 1192 ms full, 70 ms incremental, 75013600 bytes measured heap growth; incremental/full rebuild fingerprints agree. A separate 12000-member cyclic graph test proves traversal without a depth ceiling. Unknown item classifications remain explicit and do not become zero escape-rate claims."
  "2026-09-06T10:50:22.629Z","harness:codex","an added SDK regression reproduced loss of a prototype-named item during incremental lineage propagation because Object.fromEntries produced a prototype-bearing accumulator. The update accumulator now consistently uses a null prototype; the regression compares incremental and full rebuild fingerprints. Malformed edge/file records, external/global exclusions, independent components, legacy indexes, and multi-file propagation are also exercised without mocking the graph engine."
  "2026-09-06T10:58:48.886Z","harness:codex","Additional manual scale evidence: analyzeDefectRecurrenceCoverage scanned 1000000 real in-memory item records including a 12000-member lineage (11999 edges), returned one evidence row, and correctly failed the uncovered-population verdict in 1422 ms with 40474752 bytes measured heap growth. This directly measures coverage, separately from the sparse risk-index benchmark."
  "2026-09-06T11:00:25.788Z","harness:codex","Measurement correction: the recurrence_index_items value on the linked unit/integration run recorded at 2026-09-06T10:59:03.787Z was attached while the benchmark link had been refused for assertion syntax. That run proves 26 tests only and must not be used as million-item execution evidence. The separately documented manual benchmark remains valid; the next linked benchmark run supplies the correct executable provenance."
  "2026-09-06T11:13:23.986Z","harness:codex","Evidence: exact full coverage passed 100/100/100/100 with 8494 tests before the final external-provenance regression. Manual SDK reproduction then exposed canonical global dependency provenance being counted locally; reused the core external-reference classifiers and verified 12 focused unit/integration tests including a real CLI external alias mutation. Global provenance, URLs, and provider locators are excluded; malformed records, local missing references, deep cycles, and incremental inheritance remain covered. Final full coverage and static gates follow on the quiescent delivery."
  "2026-09-06T11:21:57.058Z","harness:codex","Final policy-only gate passes against the complete 2650-item corpus: 135 covered recurrence members, 46 components, 92 edges, zero uncovered or missing local items, 18 seeded families. There are now 62 explicitly classified members and 73 unknown; escape_rate remains null and budget_scope remains registered_families_only. Earlier classification counts predate the new defect evidence on this delivery."
  "2026-09-06T11:26:06.045Z","harness:codex","Delivery verification: 627 test files / 8495 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, including final canonical-global provenance and provider-locator regressions. Unit, SDK action, MCP runtime, CLI, negative-policy, packed npm/npx/bunx, direct Bun SDK/CLI, and million-item checks pass. No coverage exclusions, budget increases, new suppressions, or fabricated family classifications were introduced. GitHub dependency/code-scanning alerts are empty and pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Existing incompatible major dependency upgrades and unresolved release Sentry groups retain their canonical owners; this closure certifies recurrence implementation and evidence, not publication."
  "2026-09-06T11:39:30.462Z","harness:codex","Pre-review TDD correction: a real zero-byte item document caused the new lineage SDK action to return a successful partial population. The existing assurance context used tolerant metadata enumeration. Recurrence actions and the mandatory defect gate now request the existing public strict-list contract through an additive strict_read workspace option, preserving list_source_incomplete rather than certifying an omitted corpus. The integration regression checks both lineage and cached-risk SDK/CLI consumers."
  "2026-09-06T11:42:39.067Z","harness:codex","Strict-source correction verified: the linked recurrence unit/integration/gate command passes after the zero-byte-file red test, and the real policy gate still covers 135/135 members when loaded through strict all-status reads. Both SDK and CLI lineage/risk consumers now refuse incomplete input. Public SDK snapshot and focused ESLint pass. The previous full 8495-test and static receipts precede this small correction; final full coverage and static checks will run on the reviewed head."
  "2026-09-06T12:56:26.642Z","harness:codex","Review correction: the published PM SDK mutateItem primitive appended test_run_measurement_correction at history entry 44. Current full reads and pm get --at 44 both exclude measurements from test-local-mtpp8lij-zdwitw; the actual million-item benchmark test-local-mtppafra-4zjm1p remains unchanged. History verification passes all 44 entries and current hash equals latest after_hash. No historical event was edited. Recurrence targets and project file paths are trimmed at extraction, and mismatched lineage change input is rejected."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-06T10:54:13.366Z","harness:codex","Keep direct family matches separate from inherited recurrence membership. Otherwise removing an edge incrementally can retain a stale inherited gate. Derive the coverage denominator from all recorded local recurrence components, including missing references and unknown classifications."
